Subject: [PATCH 10/10] test(core): cover multi-mention broadcast and set-based
 sticky routing
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

gatedEngine now names its engine ("my-self"): a leading run that names
us puts that name into the addressed set, and an unnamed engine would
silently skip the real path.

New in mention_route_test.go:

- LeadingRunWins: the run is read to its end (self closing "@dsh @claude
  是谁" still answers), a body mention does not join it, and both peers
  inside the run are reported as "my-dsh,my-workbuddy".
- LeadingRunSeparators: halfwidth/fullwidth commas, ideographic comma,
  plus sign, ideographic space and a leading indent all split nothing;
  a plain word and a bare @ both terminate the run.
- LeadingRunBroadcasts (cluster level): "@wb @dsh", "@wb，@dsh" and the
  three-name run all deliver to every named project, while "@dsh 先看，
  @claude 再说" stays first-mention-wins.

New in mention_sticky_test.go:

- MarkHoldsASet: dedup, REPLACE-not-merge narrowing, all-blank Mark
  keeps the previous set, and Lookup hands out a copy.
- MultipleAddresseesAllReceiveIt: the caption-less photo after a
  two-name broadcast reaches both owners, and a later single @ narrows
  it back down.
- fallbackTable is synced to the live config.toml (default answerer
  moved from the Claude project to WorkBuddy on 2026-09-20); the three
  assertions that pinned the old defaults follow.
- TestMentionsSelf_MatchesGateRule renames the positional version:
  "@dsh @claude 是谁" is now true — a leading run that contains us
  addresses us even when a peer opens it.
